r":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0085. The text-styles cache is safe and leaves the resolved styles unchanged, but nobody has measured whether it actually speeds up opening a deck.\n\n**What I checked**\n- **Rejection rules:** none apply. The Executor log is filled in. The executor deliberately requested no follow-up, so the empty Spawned packets section and `.theseus/spawn/` are consistent with the log. This is a refactor packet, not a characterize one.\n- **Scope and budget:** only `external/sdkjs/common/Drawings/Format/Shape.js` changed, about 90 lines, well under the 800-line and 6-file limits.\n- **Styles stay identical (`contract.preserve`):** `computeTextStyles` is the old body, moved without changes. The cache is used only when the cache key covers every input that function reads:\n  - level, presentation, master and theme Ids;\n  - layout Id, placeholder type and index;\n  - the Ids of every shape in the inheritance chain;\n  - the autofit values, either from bodyPr or the temporary ones depending on `bCheckAutoFitFlag`.\n- **Cases left uncached:** shapes with their own `lstStyle` level, a `fontRef`, smartArt or GraphicFrame shapes, the PDF editor, and non-presentation editors (where the document-language input applies). Nothing is cached for these.\n- **Sharing one styles object:** a cache hit returns a new wrapper with this shape's own slide, layout and notes, and the executor confirmed consumers only read styles through `Get_Pr` copies.\n- **Staleness:** the cache is used only while History is empty, so in practice only right after opening. Editing (the first history point), co-editing (several users) or a change arriving from another user empties it and switches it off for good. That fixes the stale-styles issue raised in the previous rejection. Any error while building the key falls back to the normal path.\n\n**Weak points (not reasons to reject)**\n- There is still no benchmark on `deck-50.pptx`, so the hit rate and time saved are unknown.\n- The online co-authoring check (`m_nUseType !== 1`) may switch the cache off in most server-hosted sessions, even when one person is editing. If so, the cache would mostly help only in single-user or offline opens.\n- This only costs performance, not correctness, but a follow-up packet should measure it before anyone counts on the speedup.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Cache keyed on every input to computeTextStyles, used only before the first edit and never in co-editing; styles unchanged; speedup still unmeasured.","ttft_ms":3748,"type":"result","duration_ms":25559,"uuid":"4172b2e7-4af1-4abd-bbc2-f90f9037cc04","ttft_stream_ms":2080,"time_to_request_ms":431,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":195,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":23,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":42,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":22,"init_frame_send":11,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":12,"message_prep":6,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":8,"request_announcements":35,"query_setup":6,"auto_mode_context_wait":14,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":30,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":9},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":148,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":258,"time_to_request_major_faults":46,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":213,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":222,"process_anon_mib_result":134,"process_peak_rss_mib":245,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1054,"process_wall_ms_turn":25559,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":395,"process_wall_ms_streaming":17399,"main_stream_count":4,"main_stream_event_count":264,"main_stream_chunk_count":83,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":12,"cpu_ms":21,"major_faults":4,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":8,"ambient_wait_ms":12,"render_ms":1,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_f